# Captured runs land here, one file per run, named <step>-<UTC timestamp>.txt.
# `./run.sh <step>` writes one and pushes it; `PUSH=0 ./run.sh <step>` writes one
# and leaves it here. `./run.sh --list` names the steps on this branch.
#
# These files are TRACKED on purpose: committing a log is how a run escapes a
# machine nobody can interactively reach. Clear them with `git rm ops-logs/*.txt`
# when an investigation closes - git history keeps them.
